TITLE:: Tabset
SUMMARY:: A tabbed container.
CATEGORIES:: GUI>Views
RELATED:: Classes/Font, Classes/HLayout, Classes/Pen, Classes/SCViewHolder, Classes/StackLayout, Classes/StaticText, Classes/UserView, Classes/View, Classes/VLayout

DESCRIPTION::
TELETYPE::Tabset:: is a LINK::Classes/SCViewHolder::. Its view is a LINK::Classes/VLayout::. The top region holds an LINK::Classes/HLayout:: for the tabs. Its height is LINK::#-tabHeight:: plus LINK::#-tabGapWidth::. Each tab's width is LINK::#-minTabWidth::, or the width of its label plus 20 pixels, whichever is larger. LINK::#-tabGapWidth:: pixels separate the tabs, and none come before the first. The space to the right of them stretches. The region underneath stretches. A LINK::Classes/UserView:: fills it with the foreground colour. LINK::#-cornerRadius:: rounds that view's bottom two corners; its top corners stay square. A LINK::Classes/StackLayout:: of the views passed to LINK::#-addTab:: lies on top of the drawing. Each of those views fills its page, inset by LINK::#-pagePadding::. LINK::#-backgroundColour:: is the bar behind the tabs. LINK::#-foregroundColour:: is every tab and the page area. Each tab is a LINK::Classes/StackLayout:: in CODE::\stackAll:: mode. Underneath is a LINK::Classes/VLayout:: whose top section is a LINK::Classes/UserView:: that stretches and is filled with the foreground colour. LINK::#-cornerRadius:: rounds its top two corners; the bottom two stay square. The bottom section is LINK::#-tabGapWidth:: pixels high and stays square. That strip uses the foreground colour on the selected tab and the background colour on the others. The LINK::Classes/StaticText:: label is the top layer, centred over the tab. The selected label uses LINK::#-selectedTabTextColour::. The other labels use LINK::#-unselectedTabTextColour::. Clicking a tab shows its page. LINK::#-canSwitchTab::, when CODE::false::, ignores a click on any other tab. LINK::#-selectFunc::, when set, is called with the new index after a tab becomes selected, including the first tab. Clicking the tab that is already selected does not call it. When LINK::#-addViewFunc:: is a LINK::Classes/Function::, a tab labelled CODE::+:: stays to the right of the other tabs. It uses the same spacing and bottom strip. Pressing it colours the CODE::+:: with LINK::#-selectedTabTextColour:: until the pointer is released over it or leaves it. Releasing over it runs the function, unless LINK::#-canSwitchTab:: is CODE::false::, in which case the function is not run. A returned LINK::Classes/Array:: of a LINK::Classes/String:: and a LINK::Classes/View:: or LINK::Classes/SCViewHolder:: is passed to LINK::#-addTab::, and that new tab is selected. Any other result is posted as an error.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
Creates an instance of TELETYPE::Tabset::.

RETURNS::
A new TELETYPE::Tabset:: instance.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: addTab
Adds a tab and places CODE::view:: in the page LINK::Classes/StackLayout::. The stack gives that view the page area inside LINK::#-pagePadding::. The label CODE::name:: is centred over the tab, above a strip LINK::#-tabGapWidth:: pixels high. The strip matches the foreground colour while the tab is selected and the background colour otherwise. The selected label uses LINK::#-selectedTabTextColour::. Other labels use LINK::#-unselectedTabTextColour::. The first tab is selected. Later tabs stay unselected until clicked.

ARGUMENT:: name
The label text. A LINK::Classes/String::.

ARGUMENT:: view
The page contents. A LINK::Classes/View:: or an LINK::Classes/SCViewHolder::.

METHOD:: backgroundColour
The colour of the bar behind the tabs. CODE::backgroundColour_:: replaces it.

ARGUMENT:: colour
The new colour when setting. A LINK::Classes/Color::.

METHOD:: foregroundColour
The colour of every tab and every page. CODE::foregroundColour_:: replaces it, including tabs and pages already added.

ARGUMENT:: colour
The new colour when setting. A LINK::Classes/Color::.

METHOD:: tabHeight
The height of each tab in pixels, excluding the bottom strip. The default is 50. CODE::tabHeight_:: replaces it. The value must be greater than 0.

ARGUMENT:: newTabHeight
The new height when setting. A LINK::Classes/SimpleNumber:: greater than 0.

METHOD:: tabGapWidth
The space between tabs, and the height of the strip at the bottom of each tab, in pixels. The default is 5. There is no space before the first tab. CODE::tabGapWidth_:: replaces it, including tabs already added. The value must not be less than 0.

ARGUMENT:: newTabGapWidth
The new size when setting. A LINK::Classes/SimpleNumber:: greater than or equal to 0.

METHOD:: tabFont
The LINK::Classes/Font:: used for every tab label. The default is CODE::Font.default::. CODE::tabFont_:: replaces it, including tabs already added.

ARGUMENT:: newTabFont
The new font when setting. A LINK::Classes/Font::.

METHOD:: cornerRadius
The radius in pixels of the top two corners of each tab, and of the bottom two corners of the page area. The bottom corners of each tab and the top corners of the page area stay square. The default is 0. CODE::cornerRadius_:: replaces it, including tabs already added. The value must not be less than 0. A radius larger than the area being drawn is drawn no larger than half that area's width or its full height.

ARGUMENT:: newCornerRadius
The new radius when setting. A LINK::Classes/SimpleNumber:: greater than or equal to 0.

METHOD:: selectedTabTextColour
The colour of the selected tab's label. The default is black. CODE::selectedTabTextColour_:: replaces it.

ARGUMENT:: colour
The new colour when setting. A LINK::Classes/Color::.

METHOD:: unselectedTabTextColour
The colour of every tab label except the selected one. The default is CODE::Color.grey::. CODE::unselectedTabTextColour_:: replaces it, including tabs already added.

ARGUMENT:: colour
The new colour when setting. A LINK::Classes/Color::.

METHOD:: pagePadding
The space in pixels between the page contents and each edge of the page area. The default is 5. CODE::pagePadding_:: replaces it, including pages already added. The value must not be less than 0.

ARGUMENT:: newPagePadding
The new padding when setting. A LINK::Classes/SimpleNumber:: greater than or equal to 0.

METHOD:: addViewFunc
The LINK::Classes/Function:: that creates a tab when the CODE::+:: tab is released. CODE::nil:: hides that tab. CODE::addViewFunc_:: replaces it. The function returns an LINK::Classes/Array:: of two items: the tab name, then the page LINK::Classes/View:: or LINK::Classes/SCViewHolder::.

ARGUMENT:: func
The new function when setting. A LINK::Classes/Function::, or CODE::nil:: to hide the CODE::+:: tab.

METHOD:: minTabWidth
The minimum width of each tab in pixels, including the CODE::+:: tab. The default is 25. A tab uses this width, or the width of its label plus 20 pixels, whichever is larger. CODE::minTabWidth_:: replaces it, including tabs already added. The value must not be less than 0.

ARGUMENT:: newMinTabWidth
The new minimum width when setting. A LINK::Classes/SimpleNumber:: greater than or equal to 0.

METHOD:: canSwitchTab
When CODE::true::, the default, clicking another tab selects it, and releasing the CODE::+:: tab runs LINK::#-addViewFunc::. When CODE::false::, a click on any tab other than the selected one does nothing, and releasing CODE::+:: does not run LINK::#-addViewFunc::. CODE::canSwitchTab_:: replaces it.

ARGUMENT:: newCanSwitchTab
The new value when setting. A LINK::Classes/Boolean::.

METHOD:: selectFunc
The LINK::Classes/Function:: called with the new tab index after a different tab is selected, including the first tab. Clicking the tab that is already selected does not call it. A switch that LINK::#-canSwitchTab:: refuses does not call it. CODE::nil:: means no function is called. CODE::selectFunc_:: replaces it.

ARGUMENT:: func
The new function when setting. A LINK::Classes/Function:: that receives the new index, or CODE::nil::.

PRIVATE:: init, prApplyTabHeight, prSelectTab, prSyncStrips, prSyncLabelColours, prDrawTabBody, prDrawPages, prShowAddTab, prRemoveAddTab, prAddTabMouseDown, prAddTabMouseLeave, prAddTabMouseUp, prRunAddViewFunc, prSyncAddTab, prApplyTabWidth, prApplyAllTabWidths

EXAMPLES::

CODE::
(
var tabset, window;
window = Window("Window", Rect(100, 100, 1000, 800));
tabset = Tabset();
tabset.backgroundColour_(Color.rand);
tabset.foregroundColour_(Color.rand);
tabset.cornerRadius_(12);
tabset.selectedTabTextColour_(Color.rand);
tabset.addViewFunc_({
	var word;
	word = rrand(5, 100).collect({ "abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz".choose }).join;
	[word, StaticText().string_(word).align_(\center).background_(Color.clear)];
});
window.layout = VLayout(tabset).margins_(0);
window.front;
)
::
